{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1519403-baldur-s-gate-series","id":1519403,"title":"Baldur's Gate series","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-02T01:02:19-07:00","id":1519403,"title":"Baldur's Gate series","content":"With official premiere of <b>BG3</b> - and that one I just got for my birthdays from my partner - I want to resurrect this subject on forum. I'm installing official on home laptop <b>BG3 </b>in this very moment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>BG</b>1 was literally the third game we got on our home PC in December of 1999, just after <b>Tomb Raider</b> 1 and <b>Diablo</b> 1. ( In Poland BG1 had premiere one year after world wide. ) If I remember correctly, I never really ended <b>BG</b>1, as I was about 12 yo at this time, but started it about 10 times, with various playtimes, once done maybe 90% of game. It is from Misc and Boo from <b>BG</b>1 that my nickname <b><i>WyrdHamster</i></b> comes from! \ud83d\udc39I also clearly remembered that I watched my older brother to play <b>BG2</b> in the house next door on his more powerful PC at the time. Because of this series, I run <b>Forgotten Realms</b> setting for D&amp;D 3E for about 3 years in my high school in years 2003-2006. I also return to run D&amp;D - and now Realms of Pugmire - every few years.<br /> <br /> And now I'm thinking what Origin character for <b>BG3</b> choose - or should I remade my homemade D&amp;D 5E character I played last year - <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><i>Ilrir</i></b></span>, tiefling trickster and fraud from Baldur's Gate - Cleric of <i><b>Leira</b></i>\u200b, the Goddess of Lies and Rogue? \ud83d\ude08 Maybe I will make him <b>Dark Urge</b> character of <b>BG</b>3?<br /> <br /> <img width=\"800\" height=\"1132\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/7pcbeYG.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/7pcbeYG.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/7pcbeYG.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Will probably just choose Charisma-based ready character, so have more dialogue options to choose from. \ud83d\ude0e <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Would want to choose <i><b>Wyl</b></i><i><b>l</b></i> as main PC</span></span></span>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">, as Warlock and has interesting backstory \u2013 but wanted to make him white big queer bear (like me), instead, to identify with him better. Looking for \u2018change Origin characters appearance mod\u2019 right now\u2026</span></span></span><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-02-2023, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T05:55:28-07:00","id":1519414,"title":"","content":"I played through the early access for awhile, and the game looks pretty solid. I've more or less settled on playing a good gnome druid and an evil dwarf necromancer, so now I'm just deciding what I'd like to play first. The initial intro section, with the Nautilus-class Illithid Spelljammer vessel coming down and grabbing people off the streets of Baldur's Gate before being chased by Githyanki on red dragons got me hooked, and making the game heavily focused on illithids is an interesting choice, so now I want to see where the story goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T10:26:41-07:00","id":1519639,"title":"","content":"I sadly never got to play the OG Baldur's Gate but I always wanted to. I did get to play Baldur's Gate Dark Alliance on the PS2 and that was fun, but that was a spin-off with a different style of gameplay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T17:22:55-07:00","id":1519682,"title":"","content":"And I wanted to play today before work but the download is taking too long. Oh well, hopefully it will finish it by tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T19:13:27-07:00","id":1519693,"title":"","content":"<b>Baldur's Gate 3</b> - Character creation is LITERAL HELL to me. ( pun intended) First you need to create model not for one - but TWO characters - one your Main Character - then '<a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/who-is-the-baldurs-gate-3-guardian-you-design-in-character-creation/\" target=\"_blank\">guardian' that is your 'dream lover</a>'. Then we go to the character creation itself...<br /> <br /> Only two bogy types - 'big' and 'small', but all slim. No Plus Size models ( wanted to choose as I'm Queer Bear ).<br /> <br /> And even skin and hair colors are funny. I have this darker, greyish blond hair IRL. ( Ash Blond they call it? ) I chose it on MC - but in zoom out, it makes me extreme light, whitish blond! \ud83d\ude32 <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Not too mention it took me 15 minutes to choose genitals type for character! \ud83d\ude32 <br /> <br /> And I finally chosen Gender Identity for my Him/They as NonBinary - but I did not see in dialogues any changes in text for him, like pronounce, all text is based on agendered 'You'. \ud83d\ude14<br /> <br /> Last but not least - Dear Larian, would it kill you to implement simple name generator for Races in game? I spend literally 30 minutes on name paralizis for character I could not random name from game... \ud83d\ude14<br /> <br /> Also, UI is sooo small, even on maxed text, I need to play using Windows Magnifier on! \ud83d\ude21<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200bBut other than that - Great game, great game this Baldur's Gate 3. \ud83d\ude02","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T19:50:14-07:00","id":1519920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1519403-baldur-s-gate-series?p=1519693#post1519693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Not too mention it took me 15 minutes to choose genitals type for character! \ud83d\ude32<br /> <br /> \u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the game give you the option to run around naked? I know there\u2019s the vampire/bear sex scene but I didn\u2019t think either was an available player character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T20:51:24-07:00","id":1519926,"title":"","content":"Yeah. There's an option under settings to show nudity or not. If you turn it on, during character creation you have a choice where you can remove your character's clothes and then you have different genital choices. Then with your equipment there's a little widget above your clothing option to swap between displaying your armor or your character's clothing. If you remove all the clothing then your character will be displayed as naked. During the sexual cutscenes if you have nudity on then your character will appear naked, if nudity is off, then they'll show up in their underwear.<br /> <br /> I'm kind of bummed though, my first, second and third character choices aren't working how I wanted. I was planning to go Cleric 1 and then everything else in Necromancer. But the evil god options they had in the AE like Myrkul and Bane aren't available in the full version, so that threw a bit of a kink in my plan. My other plan was to go with a Wildshape Druid, but apparently you can't initial or participate in conversations while in Wild Shape - which makes sense, but the character basically just sits around and does nothing outside of combat, and with only two Wild Shape uses per day, I can't swap in and out very easily. My third plan was to go with an Arcane Trickster, but they severely nerfed the Mage Hand cantrip from the AE, to the point that it's worthless, and Mage Hand is sort of the big special skill that Arcane Tricksters get. Just some small issues, but I'll wait for patches or mods to fix those aspects of the classes. Right now I'm playing a Forest Gnome Barbarian and just running around Hulk Smashing everything, which is pretty fun. There seems to be a lot of Barbarian focused dialogue choices, so that's awesome anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-06-2023, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T19:30:27-07:00","id":1520072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1519403-baldur-s-gate-series?p=1519926#post1519926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kind of bummed though, my first, second and third character choices aren't working how I wanted. I was planning to go Cleric 1 and then everything else in Necromancer. But the evil god options they had in the AE like Myrkul and Bane aren't available in the full version, so that threw a bit of a kink in my plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not know how else things mention by you works - but Clerics deiety is separated from Domain Subclass of it. I spesificlly respected Shadowheart from Cleric of Trickery to Cleric of Life to make her combat usable - she is still Cleric of Shar, but in Life aspect. \ud83d\ude02 ( But, people, Shadowheart of Life is GREAT! \u2764\ufe0f Making her as canonical Shar priestess was greatest Companion mistake build from Larian to this day as I see it.) <br /> <br /> Alternative builds for Shadowheart is Cleric of Light - as additional offensive spellcaster - or Cleric of Tempest or War as battle, first line Cleric. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T19:41:12-07:00","id":1520073,"title":"","content":"I spent whole weekend on playing BG3 ( nights also) and now ending Act 1 after 25 hours as Human Warlock, I plan to break with Rogue levels. Instant teleportation with Misty Steps should help me a bit in assassinating targets on first try. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Sadly, my whole main party build need to wait - as Halsin is playable at the Act 2 - and Minsc is not even seen for now. \ud83d\ude14<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bInstead, I use alternatives for now:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Karlach</b> as sexy Tiefling Barbarian in place of tank Minsc. And romance is FIRE \ud83d\udd25 with her.<br /> <br /> 2. Respected <b>Shadowheart</b> to Cleric of Life in place of Halsin. I still am a bit not convinced to her as Companion - but as healing spells slammer she is okay. \ud83d\ude42<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Astarion</b> as sexy vampire Rouge Assassins. My Main Character is also going to dip into Rouge from Warlock, so I could from time to time change Astarion from main party. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> I STILL wait for <b>Daddy Halsin</b> and new version of <b>Minsc</b> to show their writing and speech powers. \u2764\ufe0f<br /> <br /> I made topic on Reddit about my main party plan, if you are more interested. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> Concept party is called <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/BaldursGate3/comments/15i1qgo/natures_queer_wrath_halsin_minsc_party/?rdt=44804\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Nature's Queer Wrath</b></a> - as Halsin Druid and Minsc Ranger / Barbarian builds. \ud83d\ude0e ( And my Main Character and Astarion as pansex romancers - and later Daddy Halsin. \ud83c\udf08 )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-07-2023, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpat